# Bot2's Ancestral Recall has Bot1 draw three; Bot1's own Chains of Mephistopheles replaces each draw with a discard. The
# discard is the replacement effect's, so the ability of Bot1's own Chains causes it (CR 614.1a, 609.1), not the spell Bot2
# controls - and Bot1's Tamiyo, Collector of Tales stops only what its opponents' spells and abilities cause (CR 101.2). So
# for each draw Bot1 discards a card, then draws one: the Island, Memnite and Ornithopter go to its graveyard, and Tormod's
# Crypt, the last card drawn, is its hand. Nothing is milled.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Tamiyo, Collector of Tales
Chains of Mephistopheles
Island
Memnite
Ornithopter
Tormod's Crypt
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Ancestral Recall
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Tamiyo, Collector of Tales.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chains of Mephistopheles.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Choose(Island)
Bot1.Choose(Memnite)
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Tormod's Crypt
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Memnite; Island; Black Lotus
